,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-03-02T10:28:06Z","updated_at":"2025-03-21T21:13:07Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nmaster branch, should be reproducible in all 4.4 betas and rcs as this behavior never change since uid was introduced.\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhile migrating my project to 4.4, I noticed that Godot generates UID files for some scripts that are not meant to be attached to nodes. In fact, in my project, only one script is attachable (serving as an interface for interacting with Godot), while the rest are purely C# logic. Godot shouldn't track these files, as moving them cannot break any Godot-related data.  \n\nI consider this an issue rather than a missing feature because it results in a large number of UID files that no one actually wants.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCheck the MRP. Delete `unrealted.uid` and restart the editor, godot will generate a new one for `unrelated.cs`.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[csuid.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19042544/csuid.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103461/reactions","total_count":10,"+1":8,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103461/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}